& [ImplementedOperator]
  + scan_exact_semantic_anchors consumes a validated derived catalogue matching admitted SemanticFabric one AnchorQuery and optional scanner cursor
  + validate_exact_anchor_scan_result reruns the pure operator and requires whole-result equality
  + exact_anchor_scan_input_digest binds the complete query under a domain-separated SHA-256 commitment
  + AnchorScanFault preserves invalid query unsupported channel catalogue mismatch continuation address budget serialization and result mismatch stages

& [Discovery]
  + known identities gather first as ExactIdentity contributions
  + normalized preferred expressions and aliases gather as ExactLabel contributions while original term bases remain visible
  + unknown identities and unmatched terms enter the boundary account without invented SemanticAddress values
  + discovery candidate work is capped by one page times the permitted continuation count before output construction
  + explicit known identities that cannot fit that complete pageable capacity refuse rather than truncate silently

& [Gates]
  + every candidate exact-resolves to one catalogue identity entry one admitted fabric unit and one package identity
  + non-admitted lifecycle and disputed or unresolved unit states remain stale contradicted or unresolved
  + read-only effect boundary package project or namespace semantic kind perspective and instruction capability are checked separately from relevance
  + purpose is exact-normalized against declared purpose
  + use case is exact-normalized against declared use cases or structured admitted scope perspective and world
  + missing include-boundary declaration becomes an unresolved guard and omission while explicit conflicts exclude
  + protected identity omissions remain unresolved and never become implicit permission

& [Associations]
  + declared applicability executes only for exact validated bindings operations identity entries and matching guards
  + the current Slice2 projection contains no such bindings and therefore returns an explicit omission instead of inferred operation behavior
  + typed relations walk only allowed relation types in deterministic breadth-first order
  + every relation contribution preserves seed ordered relation identities endpoint direction hop count and evidence references
  + path-local node history prevents cycles and maximum depth and path count stop expansion

& [LatticeAndProof]
  + contribution value shapes remain channel-local and are never collapsed into one scalar
  + exact identity precedes exact label then declared applicability then typed relation
  + same-tier rank ties at the winning eligible tier become explicit ambiguity
  + record identities source anchors dispositions decisions omissions roots input digest cursor and result digest remain inspectable
  + the result serializer clips only complete tail candidates and refuses any byte budget that cannot hold one candidate plus a progressing cursor
  + cursors encode and commit profile roots input digest offset and continuation ordinal and refuse mutation request change root change or exhaustion

& [Isolation]
  + no lexical embedding learned provider attention bridge persistence network remote hidden-state effect FPGA OneDrive EVO-X2 or Minecraft behavior exists in the operator
  + no clock random environment or mutable global value enters deterministic ranking or cursor identity
  + direct Cantor query and iterative-attention implementations are unchanged

& [Rollback]
  + remove semantic_anchor_scan module export focused tests and Slice3 governance evidence
  + retain published Slice1 forms Slice2 catalogue derivation direct query and iterative-attention paths without migration
